commit 3cf99316894c95f271ec418b3ce864c31f436430
Author: billy needham <billyluisneedham@duck.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 00:47:02 2026 +0100

    ui, engine: show the queued answer's waiting state in snapshots and the Console
    
    Every emitted snapshot now merges the queued-answer store's pending
    records at emit time, so /api/state and every SSE frame carry the
    answered-and-waiting state with no change to super-step merge semantics.
    Acceptance emits a snapshot while a super-step is in flight, so the
    waiting state broadcasts the moment the answer lands; the resume 202
    returns the post-acceptance snapshot so it cannot race that frame.
    
    The ticket card and Detail render the queued answer in the running
    amber, distinct from the red needs-your-answer interrupt, and the tab
    status counts an interrupt as needing input only while it has no queued
    answer. The waiting state clears on the snapshot where the answer is
    processed, pushed over the stream with no polling.
    
    Also settle the pool-name server test's drives: an unsettled drive still
    writing attempt logs when its temp dir was removed failed unrelated
    tests with an unhandled ENOENT (pre-existing flake, reproduced on HEAD).

